   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo\n\n8 steps, cfg 1, euler. Leave the ManualSigmas schedule unchanged.\n\n## Text to image\n\nQueue this graph as it is. The reference loaders are muted, so no image file is required.\ncustom_size is on. Width and height come from ResolutionSelector.\n\n## Reference edit\n\nUnmute reference_1, then reference_2, and so on. Do not skip a slot. Set a file in ComfyUI/input for each unmuted loader. use_reference stays on.\nTurn custom_size off so the canvas follows the first supplied reference. Leave it on only when you want the ResolutionSelector size instead.\nThe prompt addresses the images as <image1> through <image10>. The prompt alone decides what each image means.\n\n## Prompt\n\nPaste an instruction that was already rewritten. This graph does not rewrite prompts.\nresolution is a pixel budget for the references. 1024 is about 1 megapixel. 0 keeps each reference at its own size, snapped to a multiple of 32.\nAt cfg 1 the negative prompt has no effect.\n"
   ],
   "title": "Note: Multi-reference",
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo\n\n8 steps, cfg 1, euler. Leave the ManualSigmas schedule unchanged.\n\n## Text to image\n\nQueue this graph as it is. The reference loaders are muted, so no image file is required.\ncustom_size is on. Width and height come from ResolutionSelector.\n\n## Reference edit\n\nUnmute reference_1, then reference_2, and so on. Do not skip a slot. Set a file in ComfyUI/input for each unmuted loader. use_reference stays on.\nTurn custom_size off so the canvas follows the first supplied reference. Leave it on only when you want the ResolutionSelector size instead.\nThe prompt addresses the images as <image1> through <image10>. The prompt alone decides what each image means.\n\n## Prompt\n\nPaste an instruction that was already rewritten. This graph does not rewrite prompts.\nresolution is a pixel budget for the references. 1024 is about 1 megapixel. 0 keeps each reference at its own size, snapped to a multiple of 32.\nAt cfg 1 the negative prompt has no effect.\n"
   },
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
